    [BugFix][KV Transfer] Require full page coverage for Mooncake merging (#18747)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Mooncake can publish different tensor counts for the same layer when its
    cache views occupy only part of a shared physical page. The existing
    merge check accepts the views when the backing storage has enough spare
    capacity to cover a full-page transfer. A peer with less spare capacity
    falls back to individual tensors, causing `Mooncake KV tensor count
    mismatch` (observed as `local=1, remote=2` for a DeepSeek-V4.1 indexer
    K/scale cache).
    
    Require each block view to be internally contiguous and the union of its
    byte ranges to cover the entire page stride before publishing a merged
    descriptor. Reject gaps, trailing padding, and partial-page views; allow
    overlapping aliases that cover the full page. Keep the existing storage
    bounds check and use the existing per-tensor fallback for rejected
    layouts. This is a layout check with no model-name exception.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    Partial-page MLA cache layouts publish one descriptor per tensor,
    preventing the storage-capacity-dependent tensor count mismatch. Fully
    covered packed pages retain merged transfers. There are no new settings
    or protocol fields.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - Validation reported in the supplied handoff package, using the
    original branch source and tests:
      ```bash
    python -m pytest -q tests/ut/kv_offload/mooncake_v2/test_base_worker.py
      # 58 passed
      ```
    - Regression coverage varies storage spare capacity and tensor order for
    full pages, shared-page subregions, trailing padding, interior gaps, and
    overlapping ranges. Additional cases cover noncontiguous blocks and
    mixed-dtype views.
    - Pinned Ruff check/format, codespell, typos, and `git diff --check`
    passed for both changed files. The full `bash format.sh ci` command
    stalled while installing the actionlint environment and was interrupted;
    the full repository lint run is not verified locally.
    - The same helper implementation was deployed to an existing two-node
    DSV4.1 W8A8 PD service (prefill DP4/TP4, decode DP8/TP2, dspark with 5
    speculative tokens). AISBench ran 8 warmup requests followed by all 1319
    original GSM8K test examples through the PD proxy, with concurrency 8,
    temperature 0, max output 2048, and thinking disabled:
      ```text
      POST=1319  RECV=1319  FAIL=0  FINISH=1319
      Api infer task time elapsed: 746.87s
      gsm8k accuracy: 96.89% (1278/1319)
      ```
    Both nodes published two descriptors for every indexer layer. Service
    logs contained no tensor-count mismatch, exception, or HTTP 5xx; decode
    recorded 1327 KV receives including warmup. The previous model-specific
    bypass scored 1279/1319 under the same benchmark configuration; this
    single comparison does not establish the cause of the one-answer net
    difference. This end-to-end result is from the existing deployment with
    the helper patch, not a fresh installation of this branch.
    
